@page "/privacy"
@inject DeyeSolar.Web.Localization.UiText T
@{
    Layout = "/Pages/Shared/_PublicLayout.cshtml";
    ViewData["Title"] = T["Privacy policy"];
    const string contactEmail = "dmitry.shapar@gmail.com";
}

<h1>@T["Privacy policy"]</h1>
<p class="updated">@T["Last updated: October 6, 2026"]</p>
<p>@T["This policy describes the SmartSolar mobile app and solar energy management service at"]
    <a href="https://solar.dshapar.com">solar.dshapar.com</a>@T[". Contact the service operator at"]
    <a href="mailto:@contactEmail">@contactEmail</a> @T["with privacy questions."]</p>

<h2>@T["Information used by the service"]</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>@T["Account and sign-in information:"]</strong> @T["usernames, verified email addresses and phone numbers, linked Google and Apple account identifiers, password authentication records, verification challenges, and session tokens used to sign in."]</li>
    <li><strong>@T["Configuration you save:"]</strong> @T["Connection settings for installed inverter and smart plug services, including account email, credentials, API secrets, station and device identifiers, and polling preferences."]</li>
    <li><strong>@T["Installation information:"]</strong> @T["inverter and battery readings, solar generation estimates and history, device status, automation rules you create, and records of rule execution. The service also stores export readings and electricity settlement data to calculate estimated sales."]</li>
</ul>
<p>@T["The mobile app stores its selected server address locally. On iOS and Android, it uses the operating system's secure storage for the sign-in session. The mobile app does not save the password entered on its sign-in screen."]</p>

<h2>@T["How information is used"]</h2>
<p>@T["The service uses this information to authenticate users, connect to configured energy and device services, display readings and estimates, control devices, and run automation rules. Saved connection credentials are held by the server so it can communicate with those services."]</p>
<p>@T["Each new account has its own installation storage, credentials, devices, settings and history. Users with membership in the same installation can access that installation."]</p>

<h2>@T["Connected services"]</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>@T["Google:"]</strong> @T["when you choose Google sign-in or linking, Google verifies your identity and supplies its account identifier and verified email address. The service does not receive your Google password."]</li>
    <li><strong>Apple:</strong> @T["when you choose Sign in with Apple, Apple verifies your identity and supplies its account identifier and available email address. The service does not receive your Apple password."]</li>
    <li><strong>@T["Resend:"]</strong> @T["when email verification is enabled, your email address and verification message are sent to Resend for delivery."]</li>
    <li><strong>@T["Twilio Verify:"]</strong> @T["when phone verification is enabled, your phone number and verification request are sent to Twilio to deliver and verify the SMS code."]</li>
    <li><strong>@T["Deye Cloud:"]</strong> @T["the server uses configured Deye account and application credentials and station or device identifiers to request inverter and energy information."]</li>
    <li><strong>@T["Shelly Cloud:"]</strong> @T["the server uses the configured authorization key and device identifiers to retrieve device status and send device commands."]</li>
    <li><strong>@T["Open-Meteo:"]</strong> @T["the server sends the configured solar installation coordinates to retrieve weather and solar radiation information. You may choose Use my location in installation settings. The app or browser requests location permission for that action; location is not tracked in the background."]</li>
</ul>
<p>@T["Fonts are served by the SmartSolar server. Service requests pass through the hosting and network providers used to operate the server. These providers may process technical connection information necessary to deliver the service."]</p>
<p>@T["The mobile app does not include advertising or analytics SDKs and does not use data for cross-app advertising tracking."]</p>

<h2>@T["App Store subscriptions"]</h2>
<p>@T["Apple processes subscription payments through the App Store. The app sends Apple-signed subscription transactions to the Solar server to verify purchases and renewals. The server stores your trial dates, subscription product and transaction identifiers, an account identifier shared with Apple, expiration and revocation dates, and the last verified subscription status. Apple sends subscription notifications, and the server checks subscription status with Apple. Solar does not receive your payment card or bank account details."]</p>

<h2>@T["Storage and retention"]</h2>
<p>@T["Account records, saved connection settings, automation rules, and export or settlement history do not have an automatic expiry configured. They remain on the server until changed or removed by the operator. Operational readings and rule execution records are subject to periodic server cleanup."]</p>
<p>@T["Verification challenges expire after ten minutes; mobile Google tickets expire after two minutes. Mobile sessions expire and can be revoked. Signing out clears the stored mobile session and attempts to revoke that session on the server. Signing out does not delete the server account, connection settings, or installation history."]</p>

<h2>@T["Your choices and requests"]</h2>
<p>@T["Account settings let you update verified contacts, manage sign-in methods and sessions, export an account ZIP archive, and request account deletion after confirming your identity. Deletion does not cancel an App Store subscription. Installation edits require the appropriate permission. For other privacy requests, contact"]
    <a href="mailto:@contactEmail">@contactEmail</a>@T[". Describe your request and the relevant account or installation without sending passwords or API secrets. The operator may need to verify that you are authorized to make the request."]</p>
<p>@T["If you connect the mobile app to a different server, that server's operator is responsible for its data handling. Ask that operator for its privacy policy and data requests."]</p>

<h2>@T["Changes to this policy"]</h2>
<p>@T["This page will be updated when the service's data handling changes. The date above identifies the latest update."]</p>
